# Path ownership — OWN WHAT GOVERNS THE LOOP'S PUBLISH PATH, NOT THE IMAGE SOURCES (the homelab /
# agent-runtime shape). Narrowed 2026-10-13 (operator: homelab's rule work made the codeowner a
# non-blocker there; the platform repos were the ones still parking PRs — homelab ADR-154).
# Before this the whole repo was owned (2026-08-11, the reviewer-enable retrace). No fixer lane
# exists here, so agents never author PRs — the gate only ever covered the mechanical lanes
# (Renovate, deploy pins), where a bot approval + green CI is the ruling's gate. Still enforced
# only together with require_code_owner_review=true (homelab tofu/github/variables.tf).
#
# GitHub semantics: LAST matching pattern wins, and a pattern with NO owner REMOVES ownership.

# ── The build+publish path: build-image.yaml pushes the coordinator image the loop runs and opens
# the deploy-pin PR into homelab (agents/coordinator/kustomization.yaml); scripts/build-image.sh
# is what it runs. Owned; the action-pin lane is carved out below.
/.github/           @RasmusSoot
/scripts/           @RasmusSoot

# Renovate's action-pin lane (the SHA-pinning PRs). Ownership is REPLACED, not dropped: the
# platform's pin-only-lint (required `ci`) allows only verified action pin bumps via a PR.
# A real edit — add a step, change a trigger — takes the operator path straight to master,
# where this check does not run.
/.github/workflows/

# The ownership file owns itself — otherwise the first thing an agent could propose is its own
# ungating.
/CODEOWNERS         @RasmusSoot

# Deliberately UNOWNED — CI + the reviewer bot are the gate: coordinator/ (the image sources:
# Dockerfile, the scan/session code), README.md.
